[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Saved independent-source DC parameter vectors

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Bounded target: execute unchanged pinned RSpice regression/misc/bugs-2.cir,
including its five requested DC points and complete saved-parameter/indexed
reporting program, with the established stock-ngspice observer bounds.
Reuse the existing typed immutable requests, original-source identity binding,
generated expression AST and reporting evaluator. No dependency or device
equation changes. This slice does not implement arbitrary device parameters,
future-analysis alteration, sensitivity, or broad simulator compatibility.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-SOURCE-DC-VECTOR-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Saved source settings follow executed immutable point requests
STATEMENT: >>>
Terminal real reporting shall expose an explicitly saved original root
independent voltage or current source's DC parameter as a vector sampled in
executed request order. A root .save card or an exact selector in a control save
before the dispatch shall select that parameter. A control save after dispatch
shall not capture prior data, and save all shall not infer device parameters.
An unsaved parameter query shall retain its original scalar setting after DC,
as distinct from both the final sweep setting and a saved result vector.
Each request's setting shall repeat for its retained real samples. A swept
source shall follow the corresponding point request; an unswept source shall
retain its own setting rather than borrowing the sweep coordinate. Units shall
remain volts or amperes according to the original source type. Reporting shall
refuse a missing, type-changed or nonfinite point setting rather than replace
missing data with zero or publish a partial report.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Frontend/RequestedControlReporting.cs and
RequestedSourceDcCapture.cs,
using RequestedDcSourceBinding's original declaration/origin identity checks.
Verification: SourceDcVectorTests, including independent expected coordinate
values, saved unswept OP/DC and unsaved scalar checks, explicit capture ordering,
corrupt-type/nonfinite cases, and 128 FsCheck cases
with replay 987,2026111401. Evidence: evidence/source-dc-vector.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-SOURCE-DC-INDEX-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Known saved parameters remain atomic under outer indexing
STATEMENT: >>>
The reporting evaluator shall resolve a known complete saved parameter name
as one atomic vector at every expression AST level, including the inner operand
of a subsequent numerical vector index. Existing zero-based integer bounds,
missing-vector failures, finite-value validation and borrowed-input ownership
shall remain enforced. An unknown parameter shall not become an inferred zero.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Syntax/ControlVectorExecution.cs.
Verification: SourceDcVectorTests exercises both a saved local and direct
@source[dc][2] reads, plus existing reporting/index/ownership regression suites.
Unchanged original regression/misc/bugs-2.cir supplies the independent stock
program and numerical oracle. Evidence: evidence/source-dc-vector.json.
<<<
